 "honest": [
  "the ladder curve is the E24/E27 engine's own (module import); members' monthly returns are month-end marks from panel rows, so the reconciliation row prices the gap",
  "large/small split is a naming choice (two broad-cap legs vs mid/small/STAR), not a factor-model exposure estimate",
  "the regression is descriptive: it says how much monthly variance moves with the spread, not that the spread causes anything",
  "corporate-action guard: a member month carrying a >20% single-day jump on its own rows is dropped from that month's leg mean (the panel is as-traded, so a share split or unit conversion reads as a 100%+ return)",
  "both start windows resolve to the same member months: the common-month set is bounded by sh588000's first bar, so the 2018 window adds engine months that carry no member marks and cannot enter the spread",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict, no prereg, no trial count"
 ]
